  "foreword": "No single scholar has ever seen the whole of Elysium's history — the Sundering saw to that. What follows is stitched together from temple ledgers, salvaged pre-Sundering tablets, and the memories of the oldest trees in Sylvaneth. Where sources disagree, both accounts are kept, because a world this old rarely settled on a single truth. The reader will find no single narrative here, only the closest approximation one chronicler could manage. History is not a straight line. It is a wound that keeps reopening.",
