            "For centuries they worked. They found inconsistencies in the official histories. They discovered that certain ancient artifacts contained magical signatures that did not correspond to any of the seven known divine aspects. They found a symbol — a circle with eight points instead of seven — carved into the foundations of structures that predated the Dominion by millennia.",
            "And they found a name. Buried in a text so old that the script had to be reconstructed from fragments, they found a word: Kaelgorath. In the oldest Elven texts, it was translated as 'the unremembered.' In the dwarven runic systems, it was rendered as 'the broken seal.' In the beastkin oral traditions, it was 'the one who waits.'",
            "In the year 1,302 of the Dominion, a scholar named Orin Thale discovered a fragment of text that had been overlooked for centuries — a single tablet, cracked and worn, containing a prayer in a script combining Aelindran writing with the older symbols of the Silent Ones. Over the next decade, eleven tablets were found, each containing a portion of the same prayer. When assembled, they read: 'We remember the eighth, who is not lost but hidden. We remember the voice that speaks in the spaces between. The circle was never complete without the eighth. The world was never meant to be divided. When the silence is broken, remember: what was taken must be returned. What was forgotten must be remembered. What was sealed must be opened.'",
            "In the year 1,319, a mage named Solara Venn discovered a crystal sphere in a sealed chamber beneath Aelindra — a resonance core that amplified a frequency no one recognized. When activated, the mages heard a voice: 'I am the space between. I am the understanding that connects all things. I am the silence that gives meaning to sound. I am Kaelgorath.' Within a decade, the worship of Kaelgorath had moved from secret societies to open congregations. Temples were built. A new faith emerged, one that worshipped not a god of destruction but a god of unity — a god who would restore the circle."
