            "One member survived long enough to leave a record. His name was Aldric Voss, a priest of Solthar. In a letter to his brother, written in the year 1,350, he described what the committee had found: 'He is not a false god. He is not an imposter. He is the eighth. He has always been the eighth. The circle was designed with eight aspects, not seven. Something happened — something so terrible that the records have been deliberately destroyed — and the eighth aspect was sealed away. I do not know who did this, or why. But I know this: the world is not as it was meant to be. Kaelgorath is not trying to destroy the world. He is trying to restore it. And the seven gods are terrified of what will happen if he succeeds.'",
            "Aldric Voss died three months after writing this letter. His brother burned it. But not before showing it to a friend, who showed it to another, who eventually showed it to a member of the Aspect Seekers. The letter was copied. The copy was hidden. The hidden copy was discovered centuries later, in a sealed alcove beneath the ruins of what would become Ashka Vor. It is now held in the restricted archives of the Duskward Pact."
