          "heading": "The Seven Days",
          "body": [
            "On the morning of the fifteenth day of the Month of Long Shadows, in the year 1,370 of the Aelindran Dominion, the world ended. Not all at once. The Sundering unfolded over seven days.",
            "The first day was the quietest. Tremors began beneath the surface — a steady, rhythmic vibration felt in the bones. The priests of Terravox recognized it: the god of earth was in distress. High Priest Granite reported: 'Something is moving below the surface — something massive. I do not know what it is, but it is not natural.'",
            "The second day brought the storms — not ordinary storms but storms of magical energy, crackling with arcs of light that were not lightning. The storms swept across Aurelia, carrying a sound survivors would later describe as 'the sky screaming.' They did not produce rain. They produced silence — a silence so complete it was physically painful.",
            "The third day, the earth opened. A crack appeared in the valley where Aelindra stood. It grew — from crack to fissure to canyon, a wound in the world that glowed with pale light and emitted a pressure that pushed against the mind.",
            "The fourth day, the gods appeared. Not in person, but as presences — forces of reality that became visible to the naked eye. The seven divine spires blazed. And between them, a darkness gathered. Kaelgorath. He did not speak. He did not announce himself. He simply was — a presence that filled the spaces between the seven, a voice that resonated in the silence between words.",
            "The seventh day was the worst. The fissure reached Aelindra. The Obsidian Spire split down the middle. In the heart of the city, Arch-Scribe Lyrianne stood in the ruins of the Chamber of Echoes and understood everything and nothing simultaneously. The balance was real. The seven gods had maintained it for millennia. But it had never been complete. Kaelgorath was not trying to destroy the world. He was trying to heal it. But the healing was killing it. The world was not designed to be split into seven pieces. It was designed to be whole. And when the eighth aspect returned, the force of restoration was so powerful that it tore the world apart.",
