          "heading": "The Sealed Chambers",
          "body": [
            "The most disturbing discovery of the post-Sundering period was not about the Sundering at all. It was about what came before. Across the continents, explorers began finding chambers that had been sealed not during the Sundering but long before it — chambers that showed no signs of the catastrophe, as if their builders had known it was coming and had calmly locked the doors behind them.",
            "In the deep mines of the Kharzul Wastes, the dwarven clans found a sealed chamber filled with personal belongings — clothing, jewelry, children's toys, cooking utensils — arranged neatly, as if their owners had intended to return for them. They never came back. A mural depicted a family standing in a doorway, a city burning behind them, their expressions not fearful but resigned. Beneath the mural, a single word in the script of the Silent Ones: Remember.",
            "These findings raised a question that the survivors were not prepared to answer: had there been another catastrophe before the Sundering? The texts were inconclusive. Some described a catastrophe of similar magnitude. Others described a different kind of event — not a rupture of the divine circle but a failure of some other system, something the Silent Ones had built and that had broken down. Still others described a gradual decline rather than a sudden catastrophe.",
            "The question was filed away, catalogued, and added to the growing list of mysteries. But the answer, when it came, would change everything."
