      "summary": "Civilizations slowly rebuild. New kingdoms form. Old rivalries return. The factions that players will encounter are forged in the fires of theological debate, political ambition, and the slow, painful process of making something new from the ruins of something old.",
      "chapters": [
        {
          "heading": "The Reclamation Begins",
          "body": [
            "The Age of Reclamation did not begin with a declaration or a celebration. It began with a funeral. In the Year of the Quiet Earth, the survivors who had gathered in the ruins of Solmere held a memorial for the dead. A woman named Aelith Stormborn — a priest of Maelithir who had survived the Sundering at sea — stood before three thousand huddled survivors and spoke: 'We are alive. That is not a small thing. The world before the Sundering is gone. We cannot rebuild it. We should not try. We must build something new. We must remember the eighth.'",
            "The memorial marked the beginning of something. Across the shattered continents, survivors began to organize. In the forests of Sylvaneth, Elven clans regrouped, their ancient knowledge proving invaluable. In the mountains of the Kharzul Wastes, dwarven clans emerged from their strongholds with tools and techniques that had allowed them to survive underground. In the eastern forests, orcish clans gathered their scattered members.",
            "The Age of Reclamation was not peaceful. Wars were fought over clean water, arable land, access to ancient ruins. Religious disputes erupted as different interpretations of the Sundering competed for followers. The most significant conflict was the War of the Shattered Throne, fought between survivors in the ruins of Aelindra who had developed competing visions for the future."
