          "body": [
            "The year is 1142 of the Age of Reclamation. The world of Elysium is changing. In the Dawnbound Concord, High Paladin Edric Dawnsworn has consolidated unprecedented power, his aggressive policies alienating allies and emboldening enemies. The Kingdom of Thornwall debates withdrawal. Border skirmishes increase. In the Duskward Pact, the Veiled Mother's Silent Watch has become increasingly active, conducting expeditions into remote ruins and returning with artifacts the Pact's leadership is not always comfortable with.",
            "The ancient ruins are becoming active. In Sylvaneth, towers silent for millennia emit a faint, pulsing light. In the Kharzul Wastes, sealed strongholds are found with doors open, interiors empty, as if unlocked from within. Coastal structures risen from waters, surfaces clean and unweathered. Religious leaders on both sides have received contradictory visions — some of great light, others of great darkness, others of change so profound the world will be unrecognizable.",
            "The Void Herald has been seen again. This time, the sightings are not isolated — on the walls of Solmere, in the forests of Sylvaneth, in the ruins of Ashka Vor, in the deep mines of the Kharzul Wastes. The beastkin tribes call it Vaeth'Kor's Return, and say the Void Herald appears only when something important is about to happen. They say the last time it appeared with such frequency was just before the Sundering.",
            "And somewhere beneath the world, the pulse continues. It has been growing stronger. Those sensitive to the deep resonance — the druids, the mages, the clerics who channel divine power — can feel it. The heartbeat of the world is quickening. The seed is growing. Whatever was planted in the deep places of the earth, before the gods, before the civilizations, before recorded history — it is approaching the moment of its blooming. No one knows what will happen when it blooms. But the world remembers. The Void Herald watches. The Breath Before has ended. And the Silence has begun."
